#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# moment

#% text
# `moment(d, k)` gives the `k`-th raw moment `E[X^k]` of a distribution; `moment(xs, k)` gives `sum(xs^k)/n` of a data list.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
moment(normal_distribution(mu, s), 2)
#% output
#= mu^2 + s^2

#% cell
moment(uniform_distribution([0, 1]), 3)
#% output
#= 1/4

#% cell
moment([1, 2, 3], 2)
#% output
#= 14/3

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The first moment is the mean:

#% cell
moment(poisson_distribution(m), 1)
#% output
#= m

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `central_moment`, `mean`, `expectation`
